  "term": "dextromethorphan",
  "definition": "Dextromethorphan is a compound that binds strongly in several brain regions, including the cough center in the medulla. In biological terms, it blocks NMDA receptor channels in a non-competitive way and is widely used as a cough suppressant, while also being used in research on glutamate receptors and neurotoxicity.",
